{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And if from the bird.</b> But not every bird — this excludes one missing a limb." "<b>The bird is an olah offering.</b> And a bird is not slaughtered as a shelamim." "<b>The bird, an olah offering, is his offering.</b> An individual brings a bird, but the community does not bring a bird." "<b>And he shall bring it.</b> To include that it may come as a free-will offering of two." "<b>From the turtledoves.</b> Even large ones. And since the turtledove mates with its partner, it does not pair with another." "<b>Or from the young of the dove.</b> And not adults, for the dove is foolish — it has no understanding; if its mate dies it pairs with another dove. Therefore only the young ones are fit among them. And since these two birds are pursued by all other birds, the Holy One, blessed be He, chose them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {4 "Reading משמת (mates) as from שימות; some witnesses may read differently."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:46.473646450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}